            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"REFINED\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"In apocalyptic and prophetic contexts, a beast primarily symbolizes an oppressive, anti-God political power, empire, or ruler (e.g., Rome, the Antichrist). A minority view also recognizes the use of clean/unclean animals to represent Jews and Gentiles.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"A beast signifies a nation or kingdom under earthly rule (often predatory in character), and the distinction between clean and unclean beasts represents different kinds of people.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"Oppressive or anti-God political empires and rulers.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"Any earthly nation or kingdom, and different kinds of people (clean vs. unclean).\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"BOOK_BROADENS\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"BOOK_SUPERSET\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The book broadens the primary meaning from strictly anti-God, persecuting empires (like the Antichrist or Rome) to any nation or kingdom organized under earthly rule. It also elevates the clean/unclean distinction representing kinds of people (which the consensus views as a minor, separate metaphor) to a central part of the definition.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"None. The book agrees that beasts represent kingdoms/nations, but defines the symbol more generally rather than restricting it exclusively to eschatological or anti-God powers.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The book and consensus agree on the core identification of kingdoms and rulers. However, the book generalizes the referent to earthly rule itself (noting its predatory character as a frequent rather than essential trait) and explicitly integrates the Acts 10 clean/unclean people symbolism into the main definition.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"STRONG\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"The consensus heavily emphasizes the satanic, God-opposing, and eschatological nature of the beasts in Daniel and Revelation as the defining feature of the symbol, which the book downplays by simply calling them earthly nations 'often shown' as predatory.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
